/* =================================================================
 * STORE — normalized usage rows + per-source metadata
 * Row: { d:'YYYY-MM-DD', platform, model, in, cw, cr, out, msgs, est, cost? }
 *   `cost` set only when the provider reported a real billed amount.
 * Sources: local | anthropic | openai | chatgpt | claudeai | csv
 * ================================================================= */
/* =================================================================
 * CONNECTORS — single source of truth for every platform/source.
 * Adding a platform = adding one entry here + one parser function (folder-log/local-server cards are rendered from the entry by App.ensureSourceCard).
 * folder-log fields: patterns [RegExp] (files to read) · siblings [RegExp] (extra files handed to the parser, e.g. task_metadata.json) · exclude RegExp (tested against '/' + path)
 *                    · parser 'globalFnName' · hint · quality exact|estimated|validate|none · qualityNote · paths [] · links {get,docs,usage}
 *                    · folder-log entries: srcIds must include the entry's own id (scanFiles stores rows under c.id)
 * local-server fields: baseUrl · validate 'globalFnName' (async (base) → {label, detail}) · corsHint ({base} = server URL) · optional patterns/parser for a usage-logger folder
 *                      · folderLabel (dual-driver cards only: noun for the folder button / folder status line, default 'usage-log' — e.g. 'Jan data', 'user_data')
 *   4b: poll 'globalFnName' (async (base) → { counters: { [model]: { in, out, cr?, msgs? } }, label? }) + pollEvery ms (default 60000) — metrics-poll driver (App.startPoll / _pollTick) diffs cumulative counters into today's rows, baseline in LS 'poll:<id>' = { base, counters, at } (keyed by server URL)
 *   4b: validate may also return { rows, meta?, billed? } — connectServer stores them under c.id (LocalAI /api/usage history); a validator error with e.answered = true is the server's own message (503 stats disabled), shown verbatim instead of the CORS guess
 * link-only fields (4b): kind 'link-only' · reason (one sentence shown on the hub card: why there is no data path) · quality 'none' · srcIds [] · links {usage, docs, get?}
 *                    — never "connected", no Connect/Sync/Disconnect; the hub card offers Details (modal) + the vendor usage link only
 * key-driver fields (4b): kind api-key|admin-key|cloud-token · fetch 'globalFnName' (async (key, fields, {days}) → {label, detail, rows?, billed?, meta?}) · keyLS 'key:<id>'
 *                    · keyOptional (Plan 9 B2): connectKey accepts an empty key (open servers) — the fetcher then sends no Authorization header and nothing is remembered
 *                    · keyLabel · keyHint (placeholder) · fields [{id,label,placeholder,type text|password|textarea,secret?}] (inputs '<id>-f-<field>'; non-secret values persist to
 *                    LS 'field:<id>:<field>', secrets follow the Remember rule) · sessionOnly (no Remember; key + secrets never persisted) · srcIds must include the entry's own id
 * collector fields (v7): kind 'collector' · baseUrl (the helper's URL) · keyLS/keyLabel/keyHint (the token — the shared key UI, Remember opt-in) · platform null + srcIds []
 *                    (owns no rows: every tool it finds lands under that tool's own connector via scanFiles / scanLocalFiles with { fromCollector: true }) — App.connectCollector;
 *                    pollEvery ms (default 60000, T3): the status watch App.startCollectorWatch / _collectorTick re-reads only the tools whose files / newestMtime changed;
 *                    it is the FIRST entry so it renders first in the Coding tools group
 * ================================================================= */
